+raised. Rules are compared based on their path, subdomain or host, websocket
+mode, and methods. Rules are duplicates if they share any method (``HEAD`` is
+implied by ``GET``). A rule without ``methods`` matches any method, so it
+duplicates any other rule with the same path. Consecutive slashes in a rule are
+merged before comparison if ``merge_slashes`` is enabled. A branch (``/a/``) and
+leaf (``/a``) are not duplicates even when ``strict_slashes`` is disabled, since
+each is still matched. Variable parts are not equal if they use different
+converters, although this heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the
+different converters can actually match.
 
 
